        </did>
        <scopecontent id="aspace_42535530b1b714df8a7ab19facc4d30b">
          <head>Scope and Contents</head>
          <p>Extract from the diary of Martin Boureau recounting a voyage from Dunkerque, France to the Caribbean in a ship commanded by Captain Pierre de Latre. Topics include Saint-Domingue Governor Pierre-Paul Tarin de Cussy and other colonial governors, Spanish and Dutch traders, conflicts in the region, activities of the Brandenburg African Company, and trafficking abducted Africans. The journal also makes note of other ships, such as a frigate from Vlissigen, Netherlands, and a flute from Brandenburg-Prussia.</p>
        </scopecontent>
